The give-back arm-floor forward-test is graded off `/api/health/giveback-arm-floor`. **That route cannot report its own blindness**, and it has been blind since 2026-07-22 while reading healthy.

## The defect

`recordGiveBackState(...)` lives at `packages/server/src/signal-engine.ts:3783`, **inside** the master gate:

```ts
// signal-engine.ts:3764 .. 3785
const bookMarkEnv = this.mode === 'live' ? process.env : this.resolveDemoFlagEnv();
if (isExitRiskRulesEnabled(bookMarkEnv)) {
  const { realizedPlusOpen, bookEquity } = this.computeBookMark(prices);
  const giveBackArmFloor = isBookGiveBackArmFloorEnabled(bookMarkEnv) ? ... : 0;
  const { tripped, snapshot } = this.riskGovernor.markBook(...);
  ...
  recordGiveBackState(this.mode, this.feedContextKey, etDateString(new Date()), snapshot);  // :3783
}
```

`EXIT_RISK_RULES_ENABLED` off ⇒ `markBook` never runs ⇒ **no session record is written at all**. The counters do not go to zero, they *stop moving* — and a frozen counter is indistinguishable from a healthy one.

